# Cybersecurity Incident & Threat Management System

## 1. Project Overview

The Cybersecurity Incident & Threat Management System is a backend application developed using FastAPI and PostgreSQL to help organizations manage security incidents, monitor alerts, track vulnerabilities, investigate suspicious activities, assign security analysts, assess risks, and generate security reports.

The application implements authentication, role-based access control, database management, incident response workflows, remediation tracking, audit logging, dashboard APIs, advanced search, reporting, and integration testing.

## 2. Technology Stack

- Python 3.11+
- FastAPI
- Pydantic
- SQLAlchemy
- PostgreSQL
- JWT Authentication
- Password Hashing with Argon2
- Alembic Database Migrations
- Pytest
- HTTPX
- Swagger UI / OpenAPI
- Docker and Docker Compose configuration

## 3. User Roles

The system supports role-based access control for security operations, including:

- Super Admin
- Security Manager
- Security Analyst
- IT Administrator
- Auditor

Additional application roles may be configured for incident response and read-only access.

